Subject: [PATCH 11154/11362] [outer-loop] The new-arm trigger could never fire
 on a default run

Round two's finding, verified before recording. _new_arm_cells gated on
set(ARM_ORDER) <= arms_fired. ARM_ORDER holds four arms and the fourth is
env-gated and default OFF, so a run without CARNOT_ARC_SUPERVISOR_TOOL_ARM=1
could never satisfy it. The trigger was structurally unreachable for any
default-configured run.

53 of 64 unredirected windows were therefore invisible to the tool that writes
the new-arm specification, which is the signal CLAUDE.md names as the written
spec for a new arm. The sharper edge: that flag is one of the two recorded as
off_measured earlier tonight, so the only runs that could produce a new-arm
spec carried an arm since measured as null.

A shadow control now exists and reproduces 12 of 19 credits with nothing
applied, which is a base rate saying most of the credit signal is not
attributable to the supervisor.

Honest null carried through rather than worked around: 0 of 28 eval rows carry
the REQ-7013 split fields, so retire-or-promote by sole credit is not decidable
on existing evidence, and no arm was retired or promoted.

Verified rather than relayed: commit present, worktree clean, ledger numbers
read from committed JSON on both branches, and one mutation reproduced by hand
in the worktree with PYTHONPATH pinned there.

The change is NOT adversarially reviewed. The agent's reviewer never returned
and it said so instead of implying otherwise.

